// wings, and among its bigs. The All-Time pool of the College Basketball mode (components/cbb/CBBMode.jsx: the
// Current / All-Time switch on its first screen; loaded through lib/cbbLoad.js loadCBBLegends, only for an All-Time build).
// Written by the legends build (F:/bap-agents/cbb/legends: hand lists + checks, generate.mjs, 2026-11-12).
//
// ── Who is here ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// 772 legends (411 guards and wings, 361 bigs). A school sits in its 2026-27 conference (data/cbb-teams.js), so the
// wheel is the same eleven conferences the current pool spins. Three where a school has three greats at the spot,
// fewer where it doesn't, never none:
//   SEC            G 46 · B 42
//   Big Ten        G 49 · B 47
//   Big 12         G 45 · B 38
//   ACC            G 54 · B 50
//   Big East       G 33 · B 32
//   Pac-12         G 26 · B 21
//   Mountain West  G 26 · B 24
//   American       G 35 · B 27
//   A-10           G 41 · B 35
//   WCC            G 26 · B 22
//   MVC            G 30 · B 23
// COLLEGE legends: picked and graded on what they did in college (national players of the year, All-Americans, Final
// Four stars, the school's record holders), not on their NBA careers. A one-and-done counts when the one season was
// a great one (Anthony at Syracuse, Durant at Texas, Williamson at Duke, Davis at Kentucky).
// honors: the college résumé the grades rest on. years: his seasons at the school.
//
// ── Grades ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
// The current pool's scale (data/cbb-players.js): 9 (A) is clearly elite for a college player, 10 (A+) one of the
// best of his era at it, 11 (S) the best the sport has seen (Maravich's jump shot, Walton's passing, Russell's
// defense). Nine hand grades a player from his college production, honors, measurables and style; Size from his
// height and weight (the same fit as the current pool). Each has a tier from his résumé (national player of the year
// and inner circle 94-99; consensus first-team All-American 90-95; All-American or conference player of the year
// 86-91; all-conference 82-87; a small program's best 76-82): a tier's players are spread across its band in the order their own hand grades put
// them, the grades in the middle of a card moving a step at a time to get there (signatures and weaknesses kept).
// Guards: median 89, middle half 86-94, 5 at 99. Bigs: median 89, middle half 85-93, 9 at 99.
// Checked against Wikipedia (the school in his college field, his height): 740 of 772; the rest have no page a script could match.
// Photos: ESPN only (194): the game's own NBA headshot where he is in the NBA pools ('nba/…'), else ESPN's
// headshot of him (cbbl_ an NBA photo, cbb_ a college one). No ESPN photo: initials.
// NOT yet through a researched second pass the way College Football's legends were (career numbers per player): the
// grades are hand grades held to the résumé tiers.
